3. S3 Versioning
Q: Explain S3 versioning, its benefits, and how to recover deleted files in a versioned bucket.
A:
Versioning Concepts:

Each object modification creates a new version
Old versions are preserved (never overwritten)
Delete creates a "delete marker" (recoverable)
Versioning states: Unversioned (default), Enabled, Suspended

Enable Versioning:
bash# Enable versioning
aws s3api put-bucket-versioning \
  --bucket my-bucket \
  --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled

# Check versioning status
aws s3api get-bucket-versioning --bucket my-bucket

# Suspend versioning (doesn't delete existing versions)
aws s3api put-bucket-versioning \
  --bucket my-bucket \
  --versioning-configuration Status=Suspended
