### **4. S3 Bucket Policies vs IAM Policies**
**Q:** When to use bucket policies vs IAM policies? Provide practical examples with JSON policies.

**A:**

**Key Differences:**

| Feature | Bucket Policy | IAM Policy |
|---------|--------------|------------|
| Attached to | S3 Bucket | IAM User/Role/Group |
| Cross-account | Yes (easily) | Yes (complex) |
| Anonymous access | Yes | No |
| IP restrictions | Yes | Yes |
| VPC restrictions | Yes | No |
| Size limit | 20KB | 6KB (managed), 10KB (inline) |
| Who can access | Defined in policy | Who policy is attached to |

**When to Use Bucket Policy:**
```
✓ Granting cross-account access
✓ Public/anonymous access
✓ Restricting by IP address
✓ Restricting to VPC endpoints
✓ CloudFront Origin Access Identity
✓ Policy applies to all objects in bucket
✓ Applying conditions based on request parameters
```

**When to Use IAM Policy:**
```
✓ Managing user/role permissions across multiple buckets
✓ Centralized permission management
✓ User-specific or role-specific access
✓ Temporary credentials (STS)
✓ Path-based access (user home directories)
